    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "okay so they are regulated and all that, but it still just feels like they're acting as a guard for the money. is there any specific reason why we can't just do a direct transfer between the buyer and seller instead of this middleman thing?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Direct transfers could minimize the need for an escrow service, but they come with risks for both parties. Escrow serves as a neutral, trustworthy intermediary that reduces those risks. It's a safeguard against unforeseen circumstances like financial fraud, disputes over the property, or delayed inspections. The agent guarantees completion of the transaction upon meeting any agreed-upon conditions. If delays occur because of unfulfilled terms, funds won't be released to the seller prematurely. Even if it feels inconvenient now, this system is built to ensure a secure, fair, and legally binding transition of property ownership.",
